    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "The strike-spawns-fan identity lands as a two-geometry composite, but the engine expresses two discrete geometries rather than a unified strike-that-emits primitive (same generalization as b04 frost-blades); the ~85-degree forward arc, the fan's 50%-less ratio, and the cannot-miss coupling are un-enumerated properties. A LS player keeps melee-and-ranged-in-one-button.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-lightning-strike",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "COMPOSITE melee->projectile STRIKE (b04 frost-blades precedent: one source skill = two engine geometries, melee leads per s7.2). The FORWARD ~85-degree fan (vs frost-blades' behind-target fan) is the directional signature; multi_projectile carries the fan, direction noted. 50% phys->lightning -> ELEMENT_CONVERSION_PHYSICAL (partial-conversion attack, b04 ice-shot/molten-class routing); GEOMETRY_PROPAGATION_cascade routes the hit-spawns-projectiles propagation identity (b04 frost-blades exact precedent). PoE shock -> sunder on both components. Eras 1.x;3.20+ CONFIRMED (introduced 0.9.6; 3.20 reduced projectile count -- the 3-base count mapped is the modern verified number). The cannot-miss-if-melee-connects guarantee and the 50%-less fan damage are behavioral/numeric riders with no carriers (noted).",
      "motion_frame": "melee-and-ranged in one button: strike the front enemy, the hit throws a forward fan of lightning bolts through the pack -- close-range commitment with projected clear, at full run between packs",
